.page convert 1 convert, resize and rotate pictures

# SYNOPSIS
*convert* [_OPTIONS_] _INPUT_ _OUTPUT_

# DESCRIPTION
`convert` reads a picture (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, PNM or TGA; the first frame of an animated GIF), applies the transformations asked for and writes it as PNG, BMP or PPM, chosen by the ending of _OUTPUT_ (*.png*, *.bmp*, *.ppm*). Transparency is kept in PNG and 32-bit BMP and flattened onto a background colour for PPM. Rotating and flipping come first, then resizing.

Shrinking averages the pixels each new pixel covers (no jagged edges); enlarging interpolates between neighbours.

# OPTIONS
@ *-resize* _W_x_H_
    Make the picture exactly that size, ignoring its proportions.
@ *-fit* _W_x_H_
    Shrink it, keeping the proportions, until it fits inside that box. A picture that already fits is not enlarged.
@ *-scale* _N_
    Scale both sides to _N_ percent.
@ *-rotate* _90|180|270_
    Rotate clockwise.
@ *-flip*
    Mirror top to bottom.
@ *-flop*
    Mirror left to right.
@ *-level* _N_
    PNG compression, 0 (none) to 9 (smallest, slowest). The default is 6.
@ *-background* _RRGGBB_
    The colour behind transparent pixels when writing PPM (default white).

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if the input cannot be read or the output cannot be written, 2 for bad usage.

# EXAMPLES
    convert photo.jpg -fit 320x240 thumb.png
    convert scan.bmp -rotate 90 scan.png
    convert logo.png -background 000000 logo.ppm

# SEE ALSO
imginfo(1), gallery(1)
